<?php

namespace App\Libraries;

/**
 * Second batch of built-in knowledge (glossary, every report form, bonding fields, printing, InterLink details,
 * Designer, account, troubleshooting, using the assistant). Loaded by `php spark brain:seed` together with BrainSeed.
 */
class BrainSeed2
{
    /** @return list<array<string,mixed>> */
    public static function all(): array
    {
        $o = static fn (string $label, string $url, bool $admin = false): array => ['type' => 'open', 'label' => $label, 'url' => $url] + ($admin ? ['role' => 'admin'] : []);
        $k = static fn (string $title, string $keywords, string $body, array $steps = [], array $extra = []): array => array_merge(['title' => $title, 'keywords' => $keywords, 'body' => $body, 'steps' => $steps], $extra);
        $dtr = ['page_match' => 'dtr'];

        return [
            // ================================================================== glossary
            $k('What is a Lab Reference No. (LabRefNo)?', 'lab ref, labrefno, lab reference number, what is lab ref, reference number, sample number, lab number', 'The Lab Reference No. is the unique number of one test sample in the lab, for example DTP20261012FAA8-L. It starts with the lab code and the date (DTP + year month day), then letters and a number, and for shoes ends with -L (left) or -R (right). The machine file, the report and InterLink all use it to find the same sample.', [], $dtr),
            $k('What is a TR No. (Test Report No.)?', 'tr no, tr number, test report number, tr, report number', 'The TR No. is the Test Report number printed on the report and used when the result is sent to InterLink. It is separate from the Lab Reference No. and is entered in the report header.', [], $dtr),
            $k('What is MTL?', 'mtl, mtl number, mtl no, material number, what is mtl', 'MTL is the material number from the DSR (the style development record). Type the MTL # in the sample section and the DSR details (style number, description, component, VF material code) are looked up for you.', [], $dtr),
            $k('What is DSR?', 'dsr, what is dsr, style record, dsr lookup, development sample request', 'DSR is the master list of styles and materials (style number, description, component or location, VF material code, internal name, colour). NEXUS-L reads it to fill the sample details of a report automatically.', [], $dtr),
            $k('What is U60?', 'u60, what is u60, bonding machine, peel machine, whole shoe bonding machine', 'U60 is the bonding test machine. Its result file (sheet "U60.xls") holds one value per measuring spot in kg/cm for the Upper-to-Foxing, Foxing-to-Outsole and Filler-to-Outsole groups.', [], $dtr),
            $k('What is a Standard Spec (STD)?', 'std, standard spec, standard value, specification, spec value, requirement', 'The Standard Spec is the minimum value a result must reach. For bonding it is 3.0 kg/cm for Adult and 2.5 for Children. For material tests it is looked up by material type and thickness when you press "Refresh & Apply Smart Standards".', [], $dtr),
            $k('What is ETRF No.?', 'etrf, etrf no, etrf number, electronic test request form', 'ETRF No. is the electronic test request form number that asked for the test. It is printed on the bonding report next to the title; it can be empty when no request number exists.', [], $dtr),
            $k('What is PO / Lot No. and PO Quantity?', 'po, lot no, po lot, purchase order, po quantity, lot number, production order', 'PO / Lot No. is the production order or lot the sample came from; PO Quantity is how many pieces the order has. For materials, type the production code and press Tab to look them up.', [], $dtr),
            $k('What is an Application No. in InterLink?', 'application no, application number, app no, interlink application, a00, application', 'The Application No. (for example A005970408) is the InterLink job that a report is attached to. You pick it in the Sync Center or the InterLink list before syncing Lab References to it.', [], ['page_match' => 'interlink']),
            $k('What do U and E mean in the InterLink list?', 'u e interlink, upload form, application form, u button, e button, click u, click e, uploadform normalform', 'In the InterLink list, U opens the Upload form (where the report result and test data are filled) and E opens the Application form (the company, product and test request details). Click U or E on any row.', [], ['page_match' => 'interlink']),
            $k('What is the Sync Center?', 'sync center, what is sync center, background sync, interlink center, queue center', 'The Sync Center is the panel at the top of the InterLink page. It shows whether you are connected to InterLink, lets you pick Lab References and queue them, and lists the live changes found in InterLink. It keeps working in the background even when the page is closed.', [], ['page_match' => 'interlink']),
            $k('What is the IQC container and material log?', 'iqc, container, container log, material receiving, receiving log, material queue, incoming quality', 'IQC is incoming quality control. The container receiving log and the material receiving queue list the containers and material batches that arrived in the lab and are waiting to be tested.', [], $dtr),
            $k('What does TAve, WAve and SG Ave mean?', 'tave, wave, sg ave, thickness ave, weight ave, specific gravity average, average fields', 'TAve is the average thickness (mm), WAve the average weight (g/m2) and SG Ave the average specific gravity. They are calculated for you from the individual readings.', [], $dtr),
            $k('What is DIN abrasion?', 'din, din abrasion, abrasion, wear test, din rating', 'DIN abrasion measures how much material is worn away by a standard abrasive (mm3). The DIN calculator in Calculators & Standards computes it from the weights before and after and the specific gravity.', [], $dtr),
            $k('What is Ross Flex?', 'ross flex, flex test, cut growth, flexing, ross', 'Ross Flex measures how a cut grows when the material is flexed. The Ross Flex calculator takes the initial and final cut lengths and gives the growth percentage.', [], $dtr),
            $k('What is compression set?', 'compression set, compression, foam compression, pu foam, set percentage', 'Compression set is the permanent thickness loss after a foam is compressed. The Compression Set calculator takes the thickness before and after (and the spacer) and gives the percentage.', [], $dtr),
            $k('What is shrinkage and how do I calculate it?', 'shrinkage, shrink, size change, before after, percent shrinkage', 'Shrinkage is the percentage a material gets smaller: (Before - After) / Before x 100. Use the Shrinkage calculators in Calculators & Standards (they exist for several material types), then press "Apply to Material Form".', [], $dtr),
            $k('What is tensile, tear and stitch tear?', 'tensile, tear, stitch tear, trouser tear, die c, edge crush, strength tests, mechanical tests', 'Tensile measures breaking strength and elongation; Trouser tear and Die C tear measure resistance to tearing; Stitch tear measures how well a stitched seam holds; Edge crush is a carton strength test. The machine readings for these are loaded with "Load Machine Results".', [], $dtr),
            $k('What is colorfastness?', 'colorfastness, color fastness, crocking, uv, heat aging, fiber rating, multi fiber, staining', 'Colorfastness tests how well a colour resists rubbing (crocking), light (UV), heat and washing. The report grades each of the 6 fibres; any fibre below the standard makes the test FAIL.', [], $dtr),
            $k('What do FBU, FBL, SHB and FAA in a Lab Ref No. mean?', 'fbu, fbl, shb, faa, lab ref letters, code letters, lab ref code, what letters mean', 'The letters after the date tell the test type: for example FBU / FBL are fabric reports, TL is a transfer label, and SHB / FAA are whole shoe bonding samples. The Lab Tracker shows the form category in its own column.', [], $dtr),

            // ================================================================== the material forms
            $k('Fabric Test Report (FBU / FBL): how do I use it?', 'fabric report, fabric form, fbu, fbl, fabric test, fabric lining, upper fabric, fabric weight', 'Choose "Fabric Test Report" in Material Tests. Enter or load thickness, weight, tensile, tear, stitch tear, colorfastness and the other fabric tests; ratings follow the standard for the material type. Weight and shrinkage calculators help with the raw values.', ['Material Tests > choose the Fabric form.', 'New Record or open an existing Lab Ref.', 'Load Machine Results, then complete manual readings.', 'Refresh & Apply Smart Standards, then Save.'], $dtr + ['actions' => [$o('Open Material Tests', 'dtr?tab=material')]]),
            $k('Leather Test Report (LEU / LEL): how do I use it?', 'leather report, leather form, leu, lel, leather test, leather upper, leather lining', 'Choose "Leather Test Report" in Material Tests. Thickness and weight are averaged automatically; tensile and tear readings load from the machine file; the ratings follow the leather standards.', [], $dtr),
            $k('Webbing / Shoelace / Thread report: how do I use it?', 'webbing, shoelace, shoe lace, thread, wst, lace test, webbing report', 'Choose "Webbing / Shoelace / Thread" in Material Tests. It has a single tensile and elongation direction, stitch tear and the standard material checks; load the machine file and review the ratings.', [], $dtr),
            $k('Hardware (Eyelet / Grommet / Zipper) report: how do I use it?', 'hardware, eyelet, grommet, zipper, hardware report, hardware test, metal parts', 'Choose "Hardware (Eyelet / Grommet / Zipper)" in Material Tests and enter the hardware test results. Hardware reports are kept in their own record list, so search the Lab Ref in the Lab Tracker under Hardware.', [], $dtr),
            $k('Foxing Tape and Heel Logo report: how do I use it?', 'foxing tape, heel logo, fthl, foxing tape report, heel logo report', 'Choose "Foxing Tape & Heel Logo" in Material Tests. Thickness, hardness, specific gravity and the tensile / elongation readings are used; shrinkage for foxing tape has its own calculator.', [], $dtr),
            $k('Label report (Woven / Size / Transfer Label): how do I use it?', 'label report, woven label, size label, transfer label, label test, tl, wl, sl', 'Choose "Woven / Size / Transfer Label" in Material Tests. Enter the label test results; stitch tear uses the label readings. Lab Refs of transfer labels contain TL.', [], $dtr),
            $k('Sockliner and Foam report: how do I use it?', 'sockliner, foam, sklfm, skl fm, foam report, sockliner report, pu foam report', 'Choose "Sockliner & Foam" in Material Tests. Hardness, specific gravity, compression set and shrinkage apply; use the Compression and Shrinkage calculators for the raw values and press "Apply to Material Form".', [], $dtr),
            $k('Rubber Outsole report: how do I use it?', 'rubber, outsole, rubber report, outsole report, rubber outsole test, din rubber', 'Choose "Rubber Outsole" in Material Tests. Hardness, specific gravity, DIN abrasion, tensile and tear apply; the Rubber shrinkage and DIN calculators help with raw values.', [], $dtr),
            $k('Carton Box report: how do I use it?', 'carton box, box report, box test, edge crush report, carton, packaging test', 'Choose "Carton Box (IB/OB)" in Material Tests. The edge crush result loads from its machine folder; enter the other box checks and save.', [], $dtr),
            $k('Insole Board report: how do I use it?', 'insole board, insole report, insole test, insole', 'Choose "Insole Board (SL)" in Material Tests. Thickness and weight use their own calculators; shrinkage has an Insole calculator.', [], $dtr),
            $k('How do I switch to another material form?', 'switch form, change form, another form, different material, wrong form, change material type form', 'In Material Tests use "1. Select Material Test Form" to pick another form. The record list below it changes to that form; the report you had open is not changed unless you press Save.', [], $dtr),

            // ================================================================== tracker and records
            $k('How do I filter the Lab Tracker by report type?', 'filter tracker, category, pills, report type filter, only fabric, only bonding, filter by type', 'Press one of the category buttons above the list (All Reports, Whole Shoe Bonding, Fabric, Leather and so on). The list shows only that type and the count is shown on the button.', [], $dtr),
            $k('How do I search by material code, style or supplier?', 'search material code, search style, search supplier, search po, search mtl, tracker search fields, search tips', 'The Lab Tracker search box looks at the Lab Ref No., TR No., material code, style, supplier and MTL together. Type any part of one of them and press Search.', [], $dtr),
            $k('What do the Lab Tracker columns mean?', 'tracker columns, column meaning, action column, form category, material type column, po lot column, tested date, technician column', 'Each row is one lab report: Action (open it), Lab Ref No., TR / ETRF No., Form Category, Material Type and Code, Material / Product Description, Supplier / Factory, Style, Color, PO / Lot, MTL, tested date, technician, status and the result badge (PASS, TOLERABLE, FAIL).', [], $dtr),
            $k('What do the numbers at the top of the Lab Reports page mean?', 'kpi, top cards, total reports, passed reports, tolerable, failed reports, master lookup records, statistics cards', 'The cards show the total lab test reports, how many passed (meet the standard), are tolerable, or failed (need retest or action), and how many master lookup records (DSR, shoes, materials, standards) are available.', [], $dtr),
            $k('Can I export the Lab Tracker list?', 'export list, export excel, download list, export tracker, csv export, save list', 'The Lab Tracker is a screen list and has no export button yet. You can print the report you need from its own preview. If you need a list exported, ask an administrator.', [], $dtr),
            $k('How do I create a new record for a Lab Ref that does not exist?', 'new record, create lab ref, add lab ref, record not exist, first time report, start new lab ref', 'Open the right form, press "+ New Record", type the new Lab Reference No., fill the sample details, load the machine results and press Save. After saving it appears in the Lab Tracker.', [], $dtr),
            $k('How do I check who tested a report and when?', 'who tested, technician, tested by, tested date, finished date, received date, who did the test', 'The sample section shows Received, Tested and Finished dates and "Tested By / Technician". Bonding reports show the technician filled from the equipment code of the machine.', [], $dtr),
            $k('How do I change the result (PASS, TOLERABLE, FAIL) of a report?', 'change result, edit result, change pass fail, overall rating wrong, override rating, change rating', 'Results come from the readings and standards. Correct the reading or the standard (then Refresh & Apply Smart Standards) instead of typing a result. If the standard itself is wrong, tell an administrator.', ['Fix the wrong reading.', 'Press Refresh & Apply Smart Standards.', 'Check the overall stamp and Save.'], $dtr),
            $k('What does Status mean on a report?', 'status field, complete status, in progress, report status, status complete', 'Status is the stage of the report. Set it to Complete when all tests are done; Complete triggers the overall rating.', [], $dtr),
            $k('Why is a report showing an old value after I changed it?', 'old value, not updated, stale data, shows old, did not refresh, outdated, cached values', 'Reload the page with Ctrl + F5 and reopen the report from the Lab Tracker. Make sure you pressed Save: unsaved changes are not stored.', [], $dtr),

            // ================================================================== bonding
            $k('What do the fields in the bonding form mean?', 'bonding fields, bonding form fields, factory, adhesive supplier, model style, color, production date, shipped date, bonding form explained', 'The top of the bonding form holds the Lab Ref No., ETRF No., Age Category, Standard Spec, Shoe Side (Left / Right), Overall Result, Factory, Adhesive Supplier, Model / Style, Color, PO / Lot No., PO Quantity, the Received, Tested and Finished dates, Technician, Reviewed By and Mode of Failure. Below are the spot tables for UTF, FTO and FiTO.', [], $dtr),
            $k('How do I set the shoe side Left or Right?', 'shoe side, left right, left shoe, right shoe, side field, -l -r, set side', 'The side comes from the end of the Lab Ref No.: -L is Left and -R is Right, and is filled when you load the U60 file. You can also change "Shoe Side" in the form.', [], $dtr),
            $k('What is the Age Category in bonding?', 'age category, adult children, kids toddler, age group, category adult, which standard', 'Age Category (Adult, Children, Kids, Toddler) decides the standard spec (Adult 3.0, others 2.5) and how many spots the shoe has. It is worked out from the style name when you load the file and can be changed in the form.', [], $dtr),
            $k('How do I recalculate the bonding spots and result?', 'recalculate spots, recalculate bonding, recalc result, min max average bonding, spot result recalculate', 'Press "Recalculate Spots & Result" in the bonding form. Min, Max and Average of UTF, FTO and FiTO and the PASS / TOLERABLE / FAIL results are recomputed from the spot values.', [], $dtr),
            $k('How do I enter or correct a bonding spot value by hand?', 'edit spot value, change spot, correct spot, type spot value, manual spot, spot table edit', 'Type the value in the spot table (UTF, FTO or FiTO column) and press "Recalculate Spots & Result", then Save. Use machine values wherever possible.', [], $dtr),
            $k('Which shoe diagram is used for my report?', 'shoe diagram, which diagram, 27 points diagram, sketch, points sketch, diagram selection, 26 to 34 points', 'The diagram is chosen automatically from the highest UTF spot that has a value: a report with 27 spots uses the 27-point diagram. Diagrams exist for 26 to 34 points.', [], $dtr),
            $k('What is the Mode of Failure in bonding?', 'mode of failure, failure mode, af cf pf sf, adhesive failure, cohesive failure, possible cause, failure cause', 'Mode of Failure describes how the bond failed: AF (adhesive failure), CF (cohesive failure), PF (primer failure) or SF (substrate failure). The report also lists the possible causes of poor bonding for reference.', [], $dtr),
            $k('What is the Reviewed By field?', 'reviewed by, reviewer, review name, approved by, review bonding', 'Reviewed By records who checked the bonding report. Fill it after you have verified the values.', [], $dtr),
            $k('How do I find a bonding report by shoe style?', 'find bonding by style, bonding style search, search model, bonding model, find shoe report', 'In the Lab Tracker press "Whole Shoe Bonding" and type part of the style name (for example "Old Skool") in the search box.', [], $dtr),
            $k('Why is the bonding result TOLERABLE?', 'bonding tolerable, why tolerable, tolerable bonding, between pass and fail, tol result', 'TOLERABLE means at least one group has spots below the standard but still inside the tolerance (Adult 2.4 to 2.99; Children 2.0 to 2.49; filler 0.8 to 0.99), and none is below tolerance. The worst spot decides.', [], $dtr),
            $k('How do I print the left and right bonding reports?', 'print left right, print both shoes, left and right report, print left report, print right report', 'The side is part of the Lab Ref No. (-L / -R), so each side is its own report. Open the left report, print or download its PDF, then open the right report and do the same.', [], $dtr),

            // ================================================================== printing and pdf
            $k('How do I save a report as a PDF to send by email?', 'pdf to email, send report pdf, email report, save pdf file, share report pdf, attach pdf', 'Open the report preview and press "Download PDF". The file is saved to your Downloads folder and can be attached to an email.', [], $dtr),
            $k('Where is my downloaded PDF?', 'where is my downloaded pdf, where did my pdf go, find my downloaded pdf, where is pdf, downloaded pdf location, download folder, find pdf, pdf saved where', 'The browser saves it in your Downloads folder (check the download list in the browser, Ctrl + J). The file is named after the report, for example "Whole Shoe Bonding Test Report - DTP20261012FAA8-L (Left).pdf".', [], $dtr),
            $k('Download PDF takes a few seconds', 'pdf slow, download pdf slow, pdf takes time, pdf waiting, pdf button disabled creating', 'Creating the PDF takes about 2 to 5 seconds because the server renders the sheet. The button shows "Creating PDF…" until it is ready; do not press it again.', [], $dtr + ['diagnose' => 'pdf_engine']),
            $k('How do I print on A4 paper correctly?', 'print a4, paper size, print settings, printer settings, margins, scaling, print dialog', 'In the print dialog choose paper size A4, scale 100 %, turn off "Headers and footers". The sheet already fits one A4 page with narrow margins.', [], $dtr),
            $k('The preview shows but the Print button does nothing', 'print button nothing, print not working, print dialog not opening, print blocked, popup blocked print', 'Allow pop-ups for NEXUS-L in your browser and reload with Ctrl + F5. If the print dialog still does not open, use "Download PDF" and print the PDF.', [], $dtr),
            $k('The text on the report is too small', 'report text small, small print, tiny text, font too small report, cannot read report', 'To fit one A4 page the sheet is scaled down. Zoom into the PDF, or ask an administrator to move the items in the Report Designer to make more room.', [], $dtr),
            $k('The report preview does not open', 'preview not opening, preview blank, no preview, preview fails, preview window nothing', 'Reload with Ctrl + F5 and open the report again; make sure a Lab Reference is loaded in the form. If it still does not open, tell an administrator which report it was.', [], $dtr),
            $k('How do I get the official Access-style PDF?', 'access style pdf, original pdf, old report pdf, official layout, access report layout', '"Download Official PDF" in the bonding preview uses the original report design. If it fails, "Download PDF" gives the same sheet from NEXUS-L with both logos.', [], $dtr + ['diagnose' => 'pdf_engine']),

            // ================================================================== interlink details
            $k('How do I find an application in InterLink Sync?', 'find application, search interlink, interlink search, search application, filter interlink grid, find a00', 'Use the filter boxes above the InterLink list (Application No., style, status and so on) and the page buttons. The list shows the live InterLink rows, 15 per page.', [], ['page_match' => 'interlink']),
            $k('How many applications does InterLink show?', 'how many applications, total applications, interlink total, pending upload, synced to interlink, counters', 'The cards at the top of the InterLink page show the applications known to NEXUS-L, how many are waiting for upload and how many are synced. The list itself shows pages of live InterLink rows.', [], ['page_match' => 'interlink']),
            $k('What are Company Reports in InterLink Sync?', 'company reports, company report, manage reports, reports button, report manager', 'Company Reports lists the report records NEXUS-L keeps for the company (Application No., report no., result, who synced and when) so you can review and edit them.', [], ['page_match' => 'interlink']),
            $k('What is Sync History?', 'sync history, history sync, sync log, who synced, previous syncs, sync records', 'Sync History lists every sync action: which Application No. and report, how (portal sync or background queue), who did it and when.', [], ['page_match' => 'interlink']),
            $k('How do I choose a Lab Reference inside the pre-sync dialog?', 'pick lab ref dialog, select labref dialog, lab reference combo, filter lab report category, quick search labref', 'In the dialog use "Filter Lab Report Category" and "Quick Search" to narrow the list, then choose the Lab Reference. Its details, test items and readings fill the dialog automatically.', [], ['page_match' => 'interlink']),
            $k('What does "Select All Fields" do in the sync dialog?', 'select all fields, sync fields tick, fields to sync, untick fields, field mapping, which fields sync', 'It ticks every InterLink form field to be filled. Untick a field to leave it unchanged in InterLink, and edit any value in the right-hand column before confirming.', [], ['page_match' => 'interlink']),
            $k('What is the difference between Confirm & Fill Form and 1-Click Send?', 'confirm and fill form, one click send, 1-click send report, send report, fill form only, send live', '"Confirm & Fill Form" fills the chosen values into the InterLink form shown in NEXUS-L so you can review them. "Confirm, Fill & 1-Click Send Report" also prepares the live send. Review the values first: sending is your decision.', [], ['page_match' => 'interlink']),
            $k('InterLink says Connected but the list is empty', 'interlink empty list, no rows interlink, list not loading, grid empty, no applications shown, interlink grid blank', 'Press "Run now" in the Sync Center and reload the page. If the status is Connected and the list is still empty, InterLink may be slow: wait a minute. If it stays empty, tell an administrator.', [], ['page_match' => 'interlink', 'diagnose' => 'interlink_session']),
            $k('How often does the Sync Center check InterLink?', 'how often sync, refresh interval, check frequency, realtime interlink, update speed interlink, how fast', 'The background worker checks InterLink about once a minute, so changes by other users show within a minute. The page itself refreshes its view every 15 seconds while it is open.', [], ['page_match' => 'interlink', 'diagnose' => 'worker']),
            $k('Can I sync many Lab References at once?', 'sync many, bulk sync, multiple lab refs, select many, queue many, sync several reports', 'Yes. In the Sync Center tick many Lab References (or use the select-all box), enter the Application No. and press "Queue selected". Items already queued for the same application are skipped.', [], ['page_match' => 'interlink']),
            $k('How do I cancel a queued Lab Reference?', 'cancel queue, remove from queue, undo queue, stop sync item, cancel sync', 'In the Queue box press the ✕ button next to a waiting or failed item. Items already prepared cannot be cancelled.', [], ['page_match' => 'interlink']),
            $k('Why did a queue item fail?', 'queue failed, failed item, sync failed, why failed, failed status, error queue item', 'Hover over the status to read the reason. Common causes: the InterLink session ended (sign in again) or the data for that Lab Reference is incomplete. Failed items are retried up to 3 times.', [], ['page_match' => 'interlink', 'diagnose' => 'interlink_session']),
            $k('Does the Sync Center write results into InterLink by itself?', 'writes into interlink, auto submit, automatic send, submit to interlink, does it send, automatic upload', 'No. The queue prepares and logs the data for the InterLink form. Entering and sending it in the InterLink form is still done by a person using the Pre-Sync dialog.', [], ['page_match' => 'interlink']),
            $k('What does the red banner in the Sync Center mean?', 'red banner, session ended banner, yellow banner, worker warning, sync center warning, banner meaning', 'Red: the InterLink session ended, press "Sign in to InterLink". Yellow: the background worker has not checked InterLink for a while, so syncing only happens when you press "Run now"; an administrator should start the scheduled task.', [], ['page_match' => 'interlink', 'diagnose' => 'worker']),
            $k('What does Paste cookie do in the Sync Center?', 'paste cookie, cookie, manual connect, connect with cookie, interlink cookie', 'It is the advanced way to connect: paste the InterLink "Cookie" request header copied from the browser tools. Normally use "Sign in to InterLink" instead, which needs no pasting. Never share a cookie with anyone: it works like a password.', [], ['page_match' => 'interlink']),
            $k('What does Disconnect do in the Sync Center?', 'disconnect interlink, remove session, disconnect session, forget interlink, sign out interlink', 'Disconnect forgets the stored InterLink session. Queued items stay in the queue and continue when you connect again.', [], ['page_match' => 'interlink']),

            // ================================================================== designer and admin
            $k('How do I choose which preview record the Designer shows?', 'preview record designer, sample values, designer preview, real values designer, record picker designer', 'In Report Designer > Shoe diagram use "Preview record" to show the real values of a report on the diagram, so you can see how they sit on the shoe. "(sample values)" shows demo numbers.', [], ['role_min' => 'admin', 'page_match' => 'designer']),
            $k('How do I move all the points at once in the Designer?', 'move all points, shift all, move everything, offset points, whole diagram move', 'Under "Whole diagram" type the X and Y shift in percent and press "Apply move". Every point box shifts together; "Show all points" un-hides hidden ones.', [], ['role_min' => 'admin', 'page_match' => 'designer']),
            $k('How do I hide or swap a point in the Designer?', 'hide point, swap point, swap numbers, hide value on report, change point number', 'Select a point, then tick "Hide this point in the report" or type another point number in "Swap place with point #" and press Swap. Save layout to apply.', [], ['role_min' => 'admin', 'page_match' => 'designer']),
            $k('How do I resize a value box on the shoe diagram?', 'resize box, bigger box, smaller box, font size points, change box size, point size', 'Select the box and drag the small square at its corner, or type Width and Height (in percent) in the side panel. Arrow keys nudge it (Shift for bigger steps).', [], ['role_min' => 'admin', 'page_match' => 'designer']),
            $k('How do I test an Excel reader before saving?', 'test reader, test excel reader, reader test, try reader, preview excel, check reader', 'In Excel readers type a Lab Ref No. at the top, press "Preview file" to see the real machine file, then "Test" on the reader to see exactly which values would load. Nothing changes until you press "Save readers".', [], ['role_min' => 'admin', 'page_match' => 'designer']),
            $k('How do I add an Excel reader for a new machine file layout?', 'add reader, new reader, new excel layout, new machine format, new file type, add file type', 'Press "+ Add reader (file type)", set the machine folder and sheet, add rules (fixed cell, column of values, rows labelled M1 M2, label with value next to it), test with a real Lab Ref No., then Save readers.', [], ['role_min' => 'admin', 'page_match' => 'designer']),
            $k('How do I add the equipment code to technician list?', 'equipment code technician, add technician, technician list, qc equipment, machine technician, who runs machine', 'In Report Designer > File locations add the equipment code (for example DTP-QC-001) and the technician name in "Equipment code to technician", then Save location. Loading a U60 file then fills the technician automatically.', [], ['role_min' => 'admin', 'page_match' => 'designer']),
            $k('How do I test the machine files location?', 'test location, machine location test, share reachable, check files location, location files found', 'In Report Designer > File locations press "Test location". It says whether the location is reachable and lists every report folder with the number of files and the date of the latest file.', [], ['role_min' => 'admin', 'page_match' => 'designer', 'diagnose' => 'machine_share']),
            $k('How do I add a custom field to the bonding form?', 'custom field, add field bonding, extra field, new input, add input box, new form field', 'In Report Designer > Form fields type a label under "Custom fields", press "+ Add field" and "Save form fields". The new box appears in the bonding form, is saved per report, and can be placed on the diagram with "+ Value from record".', [], ['role_min' => 'admin', 'page_match' => 'designer']),
            $k('How do I put a form value on the printed report?', 'value on report, show field on report, add value from record, field on printout, print extra field', 'In Report Designer > Shoe diagram press "+ Value from record", choose the form field, then drag it where you want it. Save layout.', [], ['role_min' => 'admin', 'page_match' => 'designer']),
            $k('How do I answer a user who asked the assistant for help?', 'answer user, reply to user, escalated chat, admin reply, respond to user question, support chat', 'Open Brain > Chats, pick the conversation, read what the user did just before, write your reply and press "Send reply". When solved press "Resolve and teach the assistant" so the answer is saved for everyone.', [], ['role_min' => 'admin', 'page_match' => 'brain']),
            $k('How do I see which problems users hit most?', 'problems users hit, common errors, top issues, error report, frequent problems, issues list', 'Open Brain > Problems. Repeated errors, failed requests and long waits are grouped with how many times and how many users hit them. Press "Write the fix" to teach the assistant the solution.', [], ['role_min' => 'admin', 'page_match' => 'brain']),
            $k('How do I import many answers into the assistant?', 'import answers, bulk import, import knowledge, train many, upload qa, add many answers', 'Open Brain > Teach / Import, choose Plain text, JSON lines or CSV and paste the content. For plain text, separate answers with a blank line: first line the question, the rest the answer. Duplicates are skipped.', [], ['role_min' => 'admin', 'page_match' => 'brain']),
            $k('How do I check that the Brain backup is working?', 'brain backup, check backup, back files, mirror c brain, brain mirror, backup working', 'Brain > Health shows both folders (E:\\html\\Brain and the mirror C:\\Brain), whether they are writable, free space, and when knowledge.back was last updated. "Export the Brain now" forces an export.', [], ['role_min' => 'admin', 'page_match' => 'brain', 'diagnose' => 'brain']),
            $k('How do I check if the server is ready for users?', 'server ready, deploy check, deployment check, before going live, go live checklist, readiness', 'On the server run: php spark deploy:check. It checks PHP, the database, folders, Chrome / Edge for PDFs, the machine-file location, the scheduled task, compression, production mode and backups, and ends with READY or NOT READY.', ['Open a command window in E:\\html\\NEXUS-L.', 'Run: C:\\xampp\\php\\php.exe spark deploy:check', 'Fix every FAIL, review every WARN.'], ['role_min' => 'admin']),
            $k('How do I rebuild the minified scripts after an update?', 'minify, build assets, rebuild scripts, build min, faster scripts, assets build', 'Run: node tools\\build\\build.js. It writes smaller copies of the scripts and styles to public/assets/min; pages use them automatically when they are newer than the source.', [], ['role_min' => 'admin']),
            $k('How do I back up NEXUS-L?', 'backup, back up system, copy project, database backup, save copy, disaster recovery', 'Copy the project folder to another drive, dump the dbnexus database regularly, and keep the Brain folders (they are mirrored automatically). Test a restore at least once. The D: drive has had stalls, so keep a copy on the SSD or a network share.', [], ['role_min' => 'admin', 'diagnose' => 'disk']),
            $k('How do I add or change a user account?', 'add user, new user admin, change role, user management, make admin, change user role, delete user', 'Users register themselves. Roles (user or admin) are set in the system by an administrator. Ask the system administrator to change a role; the assistant cannot change accounts.', [], ['role_min' => 'admin']),

            // ================================================================== account, inbox, general
            $k('Can I change my password after signing in?', 'change password, new password, update password, change my password, password settings', 'Use "Forgot password?" on the sign-in page to set a new one with a verification code. If you need it changed urgently, ask an administrator.', [], ['page_match' => 'login']),
            $k('Why can I not sign in?', 'why can i not sign in, cannot sign in, login fails, wrong password, invalid login, login problem, cant login, sign in error', 'Check the username (or email) and the password, Caps Lock, and that you are using the NEXUS-L address. If it still fails, use "Forgot password?" or ask an administrator.', ['Check Caps Lock.', 'Try Forgot password?.', 'Ask an administrator if your account might be blocked.'], ['page_match' => 'login']),
            $k('What is Remember me?', 'remember me, stay signed in, keep me logged in, auto login, remember login', 'Remember me keeps you signed in on this computer so you do not have to type your password each time. Use it only on your own computer; Sign out removes it.', [], ['page_match' => 'login']),
            $k('How do I start a chat in the Inbox?', 'start chat, new chat, message someone, send message inbox, write to colleague, chat colleague', 'Open Inbox, search a person in "Search people" or press the + button, pick them and type your message. Unread messages show a number on the Inbox icon.', [], ['page_match' => 'inbox', 'actions' => [$o('Open Inbox', 'inbox')]]),
            $k('How do I create a group chat?', 'group chat, create group, new group, add people chat, team chat', 'In the Inbox press the group button next to + and choose the people. Some groups may need an administrator to approve them.', [], ['page_match' => 'inbox']),
            $k('Can I send files and images in the Inbox?', 'send file inbox, attach file, send image, upload chat, attachments chat, photo chat', 'Yes. Use the attach button in the message box to send a file or image; it appears in the chat and can be opened by the people in it.', [], ['page_match' => 'inbox']),
            $k('What do the RMS and NEXUS-L tags in the Inbox mean?', 'rms tag, nexus-l tag, inbox tags, chat source, rms users, who is rms', 'The tag shows which system the person belongs to: NEXUS-L users and RMS users can both appear in the Inbox list.', [], ['page_match' => 'inbox']),
            $k('How do I turn on notifications?', 'notifications, browser notification, alerts, push notification, enable notifications, notify me', 'NEXUS-L can show browser notifications for new messages. When the browser asks, choose Allow. If you blocked it, open the lock icon next to the address, set Notifications to Allow and reload.', [], ['page_match' => 'inbox']),
            $k('Where can I see my sign-in history and security summary?', 'sign in history, security summary, login history, failed attempts, my activity, recent activity dashboard', 'The Dashboard shows your sign-ins and failed attempts of the last 7 days, your sign-in health and your recent activity. If you see a sign-in you do not recognise, tell an administrator.', [], ['page_match' => 'dashboard']),
            $k('Is my data safe in NEXUS-L?', 'data safe, security, privacy, secure, is it safe, data protection, who can see my data', 'NEXUS-L is on the lab network, needs a sign-in, signs you out after 30 minutes idle, and keeps pages for administrators only behind an admin role. Never share your password; sign out on shared computers.'),
            $k('Can several people edit the same report at once?', 'same report two people, edit together, concurrent edit, two users same record, overwrite, conflict', 'Avoid editing the same report at the same time: the last person who presses Save overwrites the other. Agree who edits it, and reload the report before you start to see the latest saved values.', [], $dtr),
            $k('What do I do if I closed the browser without saving?', 'closed without saving, browser closed, lost unsaved, crash lost work, tab closed, did not save', 'Unsaved changes are lost. Reopen the report from the Lab Tracker, then load the machine results again and re-enter what is missing. Save more often.', [], $dtr),
            $k('How do I zoom the page if the text is small?', 'zoom, bigger text, small text, make larger, browser zoom, ctrl plus, screen too small', 'Hold Ctrl and press + to zoom in (Ctrl and - to zoom out, Ctrl + 0 to reset). The pages adapt to the new size.'),
            $k('How do I go back to the previous page?', 'go back, previous page, back button, return, how to return, undo navigation', 'Use the browser Back button or the sidebar. Inside InterLink the arrow buttons at the top of the portal go back and forward between its views.'),

            // ================================================================== troubleshooting
            $k('The Load Machine Results button is greyed out or does nothing', 'load button disabled, load machine nothing, machine button not working, load results greyed, no response load', 'Type the Lab Reference No. first (the button needs it). If it still does nothing, reload with Ctrl + F5 and try again; the message under the toolbar says what happened.', [], $dtr + ['diagnose' => 'machine_share']),
            $k('Some readings loaded but others are empty', 'some readings missing, partial readings, empty readings, missing values after load, only some loaded', 'The machine file only held part of the tests, or the rule for the missing ones does not match the file layout. Enter the missing readings by hand, or ask an administrator to check the Excel reader for that report type.', [], $dtr),
            $k('The machine file has a different layout than before', 'layout changed, file layout changed, columns moved, new format, different columns, rows changed', 'Tell an administrator. Reading rules are set in the Report Designer (Excel readers) and can be updated without any code change when a machine file layout changes.', [], $dtr),
            $k('The date shows as a number instead of a date', 'date shows number, excel date number, date wrong, serial number date, 46000 date', 'Excel stores dates as numbers. NEXUS-L converts them when it loads a machine file; if you still see a number in a date box, type the date or reload the machine file.', [], $dtr),
            $k('The values on the shoe diagram are overlapping', 'values overlapping, overlap points, overlapping numbers, boxes overlap, crowded diagram', 'An administrator can separate them by moving the boxes in Report Designer > Shoe diagram. Tell them the point numbers that overlap.', [], $dtr + ['actions' => [$o('Open Report Designer (admin)', 'designer?tab=diagram', true)]]),
            $k('The logo is missing on my printout', 'logo missing, no logo, vf logo missing, satra missing, logo not printing, background graphics', 'Logos print only if your browser prints images: in the print dialog tick "Background graphics". "Download PDF" always includes both logos.', [], $dtr),
            $k('The page shows "The action you requested is not allowed"', 'action not allowed, csrf, request not allowed, security token, token expired, form expired', 'The page was open for a long time and its security token expired. Reload the page with Ctrl + F5 and repeat the action.', ['Press Ctrl + F5.', 'Repeat the action.']),
            $k('I see a message with a red box at the top', 'red box, error banner, red message, flash error, alert message top, error at top', 'The red message explains what went wrong, for example "Please sign in to continue" or "You are not authorized". Read it, fix the cause it names, and try again.'),
            $k('The page jumps or the layout looks broken', 'layout broken, page jumps, broken layout, styles missing, ugly page, no style, unstyled page', 'Reload with Ctrl + F5 so the latest styles load. If it stays broken, try another browser window and tell an administrator the page and browser.'),
            $k('Nothing happens when I click a row in the list', 'click row nothing, row not clickable, cannot open row, open form not working, list click nothing', 'Use the "Open Form" button on the row (Lab Tracker) or the U / E buttons (InterLink). If the button does nothing, reload with Ctrl + F5.', [], $dtr),
            $k('The assistant gave a wrong answer', 'wrong answer bot, assistant wrong, bad answer, incorrect help, not helpful, bot mistake', 'Press "Not helpful" under the answer and then "Talk to an administrator". The conversation is reviewed and the correct answer is added so it is right next time.'),
            $k('My internet is slow, will NEXUS-L work?', 'internet slow, wifi slow, slow connection, bad network, weak connection, lan slow', 'NEXUS-L runs on the lab network, so the internet does not matter; the lab network does. Most pages load in under a second. If the network is slow, wait for each action to finish and avoid pressing buttons repeatedly.'),
            $k('How do I know the server is busy or down?', 'server down, server busy, system down, not responding, cannot open site, site not loading, down', 'If every page fails or hangs, the server may be busy or restarting. Wait a minute, then reload. If it stays down, tell an administrator; they can check Brain > Health.', [], ['diagnose' => 'disk']),
            $k('What should I tell the administrator when I report a problem?', 'what to tell admin, report details, describe problem, what information, how to report, bug details', 'Tell them the page, what you pressed, the Lab Reference No. (if any), the time, and the exact message you saw. The assistant already records the page and errors around the problem, so a short description is enough.'),

            // ================================================================== using the assistant
            $k('What can the assistant do?', 'what can the assistant do, what can the bot do, what can you do, assistant abilities, bot features, what can the bot do, help with what, capabilities', 'I can explain how to do things in NEXUS-L, help fix common problems, run quick checks (machine files location, PDF engine, InterLink, worker), open pages and report previews, check a Lab Reference and its machine file, and pass your question to an administrator. I only know about this system.'),
            $k('How do I ask the assistant to open a report?', 'assistant open report, open lab ref by chat, show report by chat, ask bot open, chat open report', 'Type the Lab Reference No. with what you want, for example "open DTP20261012FAA8-L" or "show the PDF of DTP20261012FAA8-L". I show buttons that open it; I never save or send anything for you.'),
            $k('How do I check a machine file through the assistant?', 'check machine file chat, assistant machine file, ask bot machine file, is file ready chat', 'Type "check the machine file for" and the Lab Reference No. I tell you whether the file exists and how many readings it holds, then you press "Load Machine Results" in the report.'),
            $k('Can the assistant fill my report for me?', 'bot fill report, assistant fill form, auto fill by chat, bot enter values, assistant save report', 'It opens the right report and tells you the steps, but you press Load Machine Results and Save yourself, so nothing is changed without you.'),
            $k('Can I talk to a real person?', 'talk to person, real person, human, admin chat, speak to someone, contact support, live help', 'Yes. Press "Talk to an administrator" in this chat. An administrator replies in the same window; you will see a red dot on the help button when they answer.'),
            $k('How do I see my earlier conversations with the assistant?', 'earlier chat, chat history assistant, previous conversation bot, old messages assistant, my chat history', 'Open the help button: your current conversation is shown. Press "History" to see your recent activity; resolved conversations are kept for the administrators.'),
            $k('How do I close the assistant?', 'close assistant, hide bot, close chat window, minimize chat, hide help button', 'Press the × at the top of the chat panel or the Escape key. The help button stays at the bottom right so you can open it again.'),
            $k('Does the assistant remember me?', 'assistant remember, bot memory, knows me, remembers conversation, personal data bot', 'It keeps your conversation and your recent activity (pages, buttons, errors) to give better help. It does not store passwords or what you type in report fields.'),
            $k('Why does the assistant say it does not know?', 'bot does not know, no answer, assistant cannot answer, not verified answer, bot unknown', 'It only answers from verified knowledge about NEXUS-L. When it does not know, it notes your question for the administrators to answer and offers to send it to an administrator.'),
            $k('Can I teach the assistant something?', 'teach assistant user, suggest answer, improve bot, add knowledge user, help bot learn', 'Press "Talk to an administrator" and explain the solution you know; administrators can save good answers for everyone. Only administrators change what the assistant knows.'),
